.Dd September 21, 2026
.Dt FSCK_EXT2FS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fsck_ext2fs
.Nd check and repair an ext2 file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Cfnpy
.Op Fl b Ar number
.Ar filesys | device
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility checks and repairs ext2, ext3, and ext4 file systems.
It is the ext2 counterpart of
.Xr fsck_ffs 8 .
.Pp
The
.Ar filesys
argument may be a block device, a raw device, or a file system image.
.Pp
The checks and repairs are performed in five passes:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
Inodes, block pointers, and sizes: block pointers out of range are
cleared and the block count adjusted; a block claimed twice is kept
by its first claimant and cleared from the later ones.
.It
Directory structure: entries pointing at unallocated inodes are
cleared, the file type byte is fixed from the inode mode, and the
.Ql \&.
and
.Ql \&.\&.
entries are validated and rewritten.
.It
Directory connectivity: directories not reachable from the root are
reconnected in
.Pa lost+found ,
which is created when absent, or cleared.
.It
Reference counts: link counts are adjusted to the references found,
and unattached inodes are cleared, releasing their blocks.
.It
Group summary information: the block and inode bitmaps and the group
descriptor and superblock counters are rebuilt from what the earlier
passes computed.
.El
.Pp
Repairs are applied after confirmation, or automatically when
.Fl y
or
.Fl p
is given.
File systems using the
.Dq META_BG
or
.Dq FLEX_BG
features are checked with the group summary pass skipped, since the
metadata layout of those features is not yet supported.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl b Ar number
Use the superblock at the given block number instead of the primary
superblock.
When the primary superblock cannot be found, the backups are searched
automatically.
.It Fl C
Skip the file system when it is marked clean.
.It Fl f
Check the file system even when marked clean.
.It Fl n
Assume a
.Dq no
answer to all repairs; the file system is never written.
.It Fl p
Preen the file system: fix what can be fixed safely without operator
interaction and abort on anything that would require a judgement
call.
.It Fl y
Assume a
.Dq yes
answer to all repairs.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
The exit status is a bit mask:
1 indicates that the file system was modified,
4 that problems were left uncorrected,
8 an operational error,
and 16 a usage error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ext2fs 4 ,
.Xr fsck 8 ,
.Xr fsck_ffs 8 ,
.Xr dumpfs_ext2fs 8 ,
.Xr newfs_ext2fs 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility is currently under development and has not yet been released.
.Sh AUTHORS
